<!--BlockML Documentation — a guide to combining inherited members

  FQN: org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a04_rendering.data.page.docs.MemberInheritanceAndOverrides-->
<docs:MemberInheritanceAndOverrides xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:docs="org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a04_rendering.data.page.docs"
  xmlns:dpage="org.blockml.bml.docgen.page"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation"
  xmlns:def="org.blockml.bml.definition">

  <baseType>
    dpage:DocPage
  </baseType>
  <is>
    A guide to combining inherited members
  </is>
  <documentation>
    Scope: combining inherited members, the override flag, and refining or finalizing members,
    grounded in org.blockml.bml.documentation.PartialMemberOverrides and
    org.blockml.bml.definition.MemberDefinition. Body content is authored in a04 from those
    sources.
  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="doc:PartialMemberOverrides" relation="Requires">
      Primary content source — override modes, partial authoring, and merge rules.
    </see>
    <see type="def:MemberDefinition" relation="Requires">
      Declares abstract, final, override, and readOnly on every member kind.
    </see>
  </references>
  <properties>
    <title override="true">
      <value>Member Inheritance and Overrides</value>
    </title>
    <detailLevel override="true">
      <value>org.blockml.bml.docgen.level.Introductory</value>
    </detailLevel>
    <pageType override="true">
      <value>org.blockml.bml.docgen.pagetype.Concept</value>
    </pageType>
  </properties>
  <aggregations>
    <content override="true">
      <composition>
        <dpage:Section heading="Two orthogonal declaration modes">
          <content>
            <dpage:Paragraph>
              <content>
                <dpage:Text text="A local member redeclaration is either new, which introduces a member and must not set override, or override, which refines an inherited member of the same identity from the baseType chain or from a contract." />
              </content>
            </dpage:Paragraph>
          </content>
        </dpage:Section>
        <dpage:Section heading="When override is required">
          <content>
            <dpage:Paragraph>
              <content>
                <dpage:Text text="Setting override=&quot;true&quot; is required whenever a local redeclaration merges with an existing member from the baseType chain or from a contract; omitting it when such a parent member already exists is an error, and each redeclaration layer in the chain must repeat the flag." />
              </content>
            </dpage:Paragraph>
          </content>
        </dpage:Section>
        <dpage:Section heading="From abstract to implemented">
          <content>
            <dpage:Paragraph>
              <content>
                <dpage:Text text="A member declared abstract=&quot;true&quot; is semantically incomplete and creates an implementation obligation for concrete descendants. A descendant satisfies that obligation by redeclaring the member with override=&quot;true&quot; and a declaration that is complete for the member kind — for example, a Capability override must supply a full implementation." />
              </content>
            </dpage:Paragraph>
          </content>
        </dpage:Section>
        <dpage:Section heading="Local, not inherited">
          <content>
            <dpage:Paragraph>
              <content>
                <dpage:Text text="abstract, final, and override are local declaration properties: each applies only to the specific declaration that sets it and is never itself inherited by a later layer. Only their semantic effects propagate to descendants — an implementation obligation from abstract, or a prohibition on further redeclaration from final." />
              </content>
            </dpage:Paragraph>
          </content>
        </dpage:Section>
        <dpage:Section heading="What to carry into the next pages">
          <content>
            <dpage:Paragraph>
              <content>
                <dpage:Text text="Readers should now know when a local member redeclaration must set override=&quot;true&quot;: whenever it refines a member already present from the baseType chain or a contract, and again at every subsequent redeclaration layer." />
              </content>
            </dpage:Paragraph>
          </content>
        </dpage:Section>
        <dpage:Section heading="Continue with visibility">
          <content>
            <dpage:Navigation>
              <title>Next</title>
              <items>
                <dpage:NavigationItem label="Visibility" summary="Learn the naming-convention visibility model.">
                  <target>docs:Visibility</target>
                </dpage:NavigationItem>
              </items>
            </dpage:Navigation>
          </content>
        </dpage:Section>
      </composition>
    </content>
  </aggregations>
</docs:MemberInheritanceAndOverrides>
